      {"bad":"The gardener planted flowers along the path. She gave each plants plenty of water. The garden filled with colour. Other gardener helped her with the weeding. The path looked beautiful by summer.","good":"The gardener planted flowers along the path. She gave each plant plenty of water. The garden filled with colour. Another gardener helped her with the weeding. The path looked beautiful by summer.","explanation":"Use \"each plant\" (singular) and \"another gardener\" (singular).","sentences":[{"bad":"The gardener planted flowers along the path.","good":"The gardener planted flowers along the path."},{"bad":"She gave each plants plenty of water.","good":"She gave each plant plenty of water."},{"bad":"The garden filled with colour.","good":"The garden filled with colour."},{"bad":"Other gardener helped her with the weeding.","good":"Another gardener helped her with the weeding."},{"bad":"The path looked beautiful by summer.","good":"The path looked beautiful by summer."}]},
      {"bad":"The shop offered a discount that week. Every customers received a small gift. The staff wrapped each item carefully. They ordered another boxes to refill the shelves. The shop was busy all week.","good":"The shop offered a discount that week. Every customer received a small gift. The staff wrapped each item carefully. They ordered another box to refill the shelves. The shop was busy all week.","explanation":"\"Every customer\" and \"another box\" are singular.","sentences":[{"bad":"The shop offered a discount that week.","good":"The shop offered a discount that week."},{"bad":"Every customers received a small gift.","good":"Every customer received a small gift."},{"bad":"The staff wrapped each item carefully.","good":"The staff wrapped each item carefully."},{"bad":"They ordered another boxes to refill the shelves.","good":"They ordered another box to refill the shelves."},{"bad":"The shop was busy all week.","good":"The shop was busy all week."}]}
