    "4.2": [
      {"bad":"The company planned a new training programme. They designed a ten-years plan for the staff. Managers explained each stage clearly. The programme included a two-hours workshop weekly. The first session began in March.","good":"The company planned a new training programme. They designed a ten-year plan for the staff. Managers explained each stage clearly. The programme included a two-hour workshop weekly. The first session began in March.","explanation":"A noun modifier stays singular: \"ten-year plan\", \"two-hour workshop\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The company planned a new training programme.","good":"The company planned a new training programme."},{"bad":"They designed a ten-years plan for the staff.","good":"They designed a ten-year plan for the staff."},{"bad":"Managers explained each stage clearly.","good":"Managers explained each stage clearly."},{"bad":"The programme included a two-hours workshop weekly.","good":"The programme included a two-hour workshop weekly."},{"bad":"The first session began in March.","good":"The first session began in March."}]},
