      {"bad":"The tailor measured the customer carefully. He needed a new scissors for the cloth. The fabric was soft and strong. He soon finished the trouser for the fitting. The customer was delighted with the result.","good":"The tailor measured the customer carefully. He needed a new pair of scissors for the cloth. The fabric was soft and strong. He soon finished the trousers for the fitting. The customer was delighted with the result.","explanation":"Plural-only \"scissors\"/\"trousers\" need \"a pair of\" or a plural verb.","sentences":[{"bad":"The tailor measured the customer carefully.","good":"The tailor measured the customer carefully."},{"bad":"He needed a new scissors for the cloth.","good":"He needed a new pair of scissors for the cloth."},{"bad":"The fabric was soft and strong.","good":"The fabric was soft and strong."},{"bad":"He soon finished the trouser for the fitting.","good":"He soon finished the trousers for the fitting."},{"bad":"The customer was delighted with the result.","good":"The customer was delighted with the result."}]},
      {"bad":"The trousers hung on the back of the door. They pair of trousers were still wet from the rain. The boy found his umbrella nearby. His glasses was on the table by the window. He put everything away before dinner.","good":"The trousers hung on the back of the door. The pair of trousers was still wet from the rain. The boy found his umbrella nearby. His glasses were on the table by the window. He put everything away before dinner.","explanation":"\"A pair of trousers\" is singular; \"glasses\" is plural.","sentences":[{"bad":"The trousers hung on the back of the door.","good":"The trousers hung on the back of the door."},{"bad":"They pair of trousers were still wet from the rain.","good":"The pair of trousers was still wet from the rain."},{"bad":"The boy found his umbrella nearby.","good":"The boy found his umbrella nearby."},{"bad":"His glasses was on the table by the window.","good":"His glasses were on the table by the window."},{"bad":"He put everything away before dinner.","good":"He put everything away before dinner."}]},
      {"bad":"The shop stocked clothes for the new season. The manager ordered new trouser in three colours. The window display looked bright. She also hung a new short in the window. The shop opened early the next morning.","good":"The shop stocked clothes for the new season. The manager ordered new trousers in three colours. The window display looked bright. She also hung a new pair of shorts in the window. The shop opened early the next morning.","explanation":"\"Trousers\" and \"shorts\" are plural-only nouns.","sentences":[{"bad":"The shop stocked clothes for the new season.","good":"The shop stocked clothes for the new season."},{"bad":"The manager ordered new trouser in three colours.","good":"The manager ordered new trousers in three colours."},{"bad":"The window display looked bright.","good":"The window display looked bright."},{"bad":"She also hung a new short in the window.","good":"She also hung a new pair of shorts in the window."},{"bad":"The shop opened early the next morning.","good":"The shop opened early the next morning."}]}
