      {"bad":"The teacher marked the weekend homework. Some pupils have wrote long answers. The class discussed the tricky questions. They could not understands the last one. So the teacher explained it again.","good":"The teacher marked the weekend homework. Some pupils have written long answers. The class discussed the tricky questions. They could not understand the last one. So the teacher explained it again.","explanation":"After \"have\" use \"written\"; after \"could\" use the base form \"understand\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The teacher marked the weekend homework.","good":"The teacher marked the weekend homework."},{"bad":"Some pupils have wrote long answers.","good":"Some pupils have written long answers."},{"bad":"The class discussed the tricky questions.","good":"The class discussed the tricky questions."},{"bad":"They could not understands the last one.","good":"They could not understand the last one."},{"bad":"So the teacher explained it again.","good":"So the teacher explained it again."}]},
      {"bad":"The family planned a trip to the hills. They will drove to the cabin early. The weather was clear and bright. They have took the same route before. In the end, they arrived before lunchtime.","good":"The family planned a trip to the hills. They will drive to the cabin early. The weather was clear and bright. They have taken the same route before. In the end, they arrived before lunchtime.","explanation":"After \"will\" use \"drive\"; after \"have\" use \"taken\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The family planned a trip to the hills.","good":"The family planned a trip to the hills."},{"bad":"They will drove to the cabin early.","good":"They will drive to the cabin early."},{"bad":"The weather was clear and bright.","good":"The weather was clear and bright."},{"bad":"They have took the same route before.","good":"They have taken the same route before."},{"bad":"In the end, they arrived before lunchtime.","good":"In the end, they arrived before lunchtime."}]},
      {"bad":"The singer rehearsed with the band. She may sings the new song tonight. The band has practised for weeks. They have wrote two new pieces. In fact, the concert sold out quickly.","good":"The singer rehearsed with the band. She may sing the new song tonight. The band has practised for weeks. They have written two new pieces. In fact, the concert sold out quickly.","explanation":"After \"may\" use \"sing\"; after \"have\" use \"written\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The singer rehearsed with the band.","good":"The singer rehearsed with the band."},{"bad":"She may sings the new song tonight.","good":"She may sing the new song tonight."},{"bad":"The band has practised for weeks.","good":"The band has practised for weeks."},{"bad":"They have wrote two new pieces.","good":"They have written two new pieces."},{"bad":"In fact, the concert sold out quickly.","good":"In fact, the concert sold out quickly."}]},
      {"bad":"The kitchen prepared for the dinner rush. The chef must washes the vegetables first. The staff have set the tables neatly. They have went through the whole menu twice. Then the doors opened at six.","good":"The kitchen prepared for the dinner rush. The chef must wash the vegetables first. The staff have set the tables neatly. They have gone through the whole menu twice. Then the doors opened at six.","explanation":"After \"must\" use \"wash\"; after \"have\" use \"gone\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The kitchen prepared for the dinner rush.","good":"The kitchen prepared for the dinner rush."},{"bad":"The chef must washes the vegetables first.","good":"The chef must wash the vegetables first."},{"bad":"The staff have set the tables neatly.","good":"The staff have set the tables neatly."},{"bad":"They have went through the whole menu twice.","good":"They have gone through the whole menu twice."},{"bad":"Then the doors opened at six.","good":"Then the doors opened at six."}]}
