    "6.2": [
      {"bad":"The pupils lined up outside the gate. Every morning she going to school by bus. Her friends wait at the same stop. They running to class when the bell rings. Then the teacher greets them at the door.","good":"The pupils lined up outside the gate. Every morning she goes to school by bus. Her friends wait at the same stop. They run to class when the bell rings. Then the teacher greets them at the door.","explanation":"A main clause needs a finite verb: \"she goes\", \"they run\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The pupils lined up outside the gate.","good":"The pupils lined up outside the gate."},{"bad":"Every morning she going to school by bus.","good":"Every morning she goes to school by bus."},{"bad":"Her friends wait at the same stop.","good":"Her friends wait at the same stop."},{"bad":"They running to class when the bell rings.","good":"They run to class when the bell rings."},{"bad":"Then the teacher greets them at the door.","good":"Then the teacher greets them at the door."}]},
      {"bad":"The players warmed up before the match. The captain standing near the centre. He shouts advice to his team. They listening carefully to every word. Soon after, the match began.","good":"The players warmed up before the match. The captain stands near the centre. He shouts advice to his team. They listen carefully to every word. Soon after, the match began.","explanation":"Use finite verbs \"stands\" and \"listen\", not bare -ing forms.","sentences":[{"bad":"The players warmed up before the match.","good":"The players warmed up before the match."},{"bad":"The captain standing near the centre.","good":"The captain stands near the centre."},{"bad":"He shouts advice to his team.","good":"He shouts advice to his team."},{"bad":"They listening carefully to every word.","good":"They listen carefully to every word."},{"bad":"Soon after, the match began.","good":"Soon after, the match began."}]},
      {"bad":"The train left the station on time. The passengers waiting on the cold platform. A porter helps with the heavy cases. The doors opening with a soft hiss. The journey was quiet and smooth.","good":"The train left the station on time. The passengers wait on the cold platform. A porter helps with the heavy cases. The doors open with a soft hiss. The journey was quiet and smooth.","explanation":"Finite verbs \"wait\" and \"open\" are needed; -ing forms cannot stand alone.","sentences":[{"bad":"The train left the station on time.","good":"The train left the station on time."},{"bad":"The passengers waiting on the cold platform.","good":"The passengers wait on the cold platform."},{"bad":"A porter helps with the heavy cases.","good":"A porter helps with the heavy cases."},{"bad":"The doors opening with a soft hiss.","good":"The doors open with a soft hiss."},{"bad":"The journey was quiet and smooth.","good":"The journey was quiet and smooth."}]},
      {"bad":"The family gathered for the evening meal. My mother baking a large pie. My father lays the table. My brothers carrying the plates inside. Then we all sat down together.","good":"The family gathered for the evening meal. My mother bakes a large pie. My father lays the table. My brothers carry the plates inside. Then we all sat down together.","explanation":"Use \"bakes\" and \"carry\", not bare -ing forms.","sentences":[{"bad":"The family gathered for the evening meal.","good":"The family gathered for the evening meal."},{"bad":"My mother baking a large pie.","good":"My mother bakes a large pie."},{"bad":"My father lays the table.","good":"My father lays the table."},{"bad":"My brothers carrying the plates inside.","good":"My brothers carry the plates inside."},{"bad":"Then we all sat down together.","good":"Then we all sat down together."}]},
      {"bad":"The gardener worked through the afternoon. She planting rows of vegetables. The watering can stands by the tap. Birds singing in the apple tree. The garden looked peaceful in the sun.","good":"The gardener worked through the afternoon. She plants rows of vegetables. The watering can stands by the tap. Birds sing in the apple tree. The garden looked peaceful in the sun.","explanation":"Finite verbs are \"plants\" and \"sing\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The gardener worked through the afternoon.","good":"The gardener worked through the afternoon."},{"bad":"She planting rows of vegetables.","good":"She plants rows of vegetables."},{"bad":"The watering can stands by the tap.","good":"The watering can stands by the tap."},{"bad":"Birds singing in the apple tree.","good":"Birds sing in the apple tree."},{"bad":"The garden looked peaceful in the sun.","good":"The garden looked peaceful in the sun."}]}
