    "6.3": [
      {"bad":"The children came home from school. My sister very happy with her test result. She showed the paper to our parents. The soup too hot to eat straight away. So we waited a few minutes before dinner.","good":"The children came home from school. My sister is very happy with her test result. She showed the paper to our parents. The soup is too hot to eat straight away. So we waited a few minutes before dinner.","explanation":"English clauses need a verb: \"is very happy\", \"is too hot\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The children came home from school.","good":"The children came home from school."},{"bad":"My sister very happy with her test result.","good":"My sister is very happy with her test result."},{"bad":"She showed the paper to our parents.","good":"She showed the paper to our parents."},{"bad":"The soup too hot to eat straight away.","good":"The soup is too hot to eat straight away."},{"bad":"So we waited a few minutes before dinner.","good":"So we waited a few minutes before dinner."}]},
      {"bad":"The waiting room filled with patients. The doctor ready to see the next person. A nurse called the first name. The seats outside quite comfortable. Everyone was seen quickly that morning.","good":"The waiting room filled with patients. The doctor is ready to see the next person. A nurse called the first name. The seats outside are quite comfortable. Everyone was seen quickly that morning.","explanation":"Add the copula: \"is ready\", \"are comfortable\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The waiting room filled with patients.","good":"The waiting room filled with patients."},{"bad":"The doctor ready to see the next person.","good":"The doctor is ready to see the next person."},{"bad":"A nurse called the first name.","good":"A nurse called the first name."},{"bad":"The seats outside quite comfortable.","good":"The seats outside are quite comfortable."},{"bad":"Everyone was seen quickly that morning.","good":"Everyone was seen quickly that morning."}]},
      {"bad":"The team travelled to the away match. The changing rooms very small at that ground. The players changed quickly. The pitch wet from the morning rain. Still, the match went ahead anyway.","good":"The team travelled to the away match. The changing rooms are very small at that ground. The players changed quickly. The pitch was wet from the morning rain. Still, the match went ahead anyway.","explanation":"Add \"are very small\" and \"was wet\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The team travelled to the away match.","good":"The team travelled to the away match."},{"bad":"The changing rooms very small at that ground.","good":"The changing rooms are very small at that ground."},{"bad":"The players changed quickly.","good":"The players changed quickly."},{"bad":"The pitch wet from the morning rain.","good":"The pitch was wet from the morning rain."},{"bad":"Still, the match went ahead anyway.","good":"Still, the match went ahead anyway."}]},
      {"bad":"The shop opened early on Saturday. The shelves full of fresh produce. Customers filled their baskets. The prices very fair for the quality. The shop sold out by noon.","good":"The shop opened early on Saturday. The shelves were full of fresh produce. Customers filled their baskets. The prices were very fair for the quality. The shop sold out by noon.","explanation":"Add the verb \"were\" to each clause.","sentences":[{"bad":"The shop opened early on Saturday.","good":"The shop opened early on Saturday."},{"bad":"The shelves full of fresh produce.","good":"The shelves were full of fresh produce."},{"bad":"Customers filled their baskets.","good":"Customers filled their baskets."},{"bad":"The prices very fair for the quality.","good":"The prices were very fair for the quality."},{"bad":"The shop sold out by noon.","good":"The shop sold out by noon."}]},
      {"bad":"The library closed for the holidays. The room silent except for the clock. A single lamp lit the corner. The books dusty after so many months. The staff returned in the new year.","good":"The library closed for the holidays. The room was silent except for the clock. A single lamp lit the corner. The books were dusty after so many months. The staff returned in the new year.","explanation":"Add \"was silent\" and \"were dusty\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The library closed for the holidays.","good":"The library closed for the holidays."},{"bad":"The room silent except for the clock.","good":"The room was silent except for the clock."},{"bad":"A single lamp lit the corner.","good":"A single lamp lit the corner."},{"bad":"The books dusty after so many months.","good":"The books were dusty after so many months."},{"bad":"The staff returned in the new year.","good":"The staff returned in the new year."}]}
    ],
    "6.4": [
      {"bad":"The town planned a new bridge over the river. The old bridge build many years ago. Engineers inspected it every year. A new design choose by the council last month. Work will begin in the spring.","good":"The town planned a new bridge over the river. The old bridge was built many years ago. Engineers inspected it every year. A new design was chosen by the council last month. Work will begin in the spring.","explanation":"A passive needs \"be + past participle\": \"was built\", \"was chosen\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The town planned a new bridge over the river.","good":"The town planned a new bridge over the river."},{"bad":"The old bridge build many years ago.","good":"The old bridge was built many years ago."},{"bad":"Engineers inspected it every year.","good":"Engineers inspected it every year."},{"bad":"A new design choose by the council last month.","good":"A new design was chosen by the council last month."},{"bad":"Work will begin in the spring.","good":"Work will begin in the spring."}]},
      {"bad":"The school arranged a music competition. Three prizes gave to the best singers. The audience cheered loudly. The final song write by a student. Everyone left with a smile.","good":"The school arranged a music competition. Three prizes were given to the best singers. The audience cheered loudly. The final song was written by a student. Everyone left with a smile.","explanation":"Use \"were given\" and \"was written\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The school arranged a music competition.","good":"The school arranged a music competition."},{"bad":"Three prizes gave to the best singers.","good":"Three prizes were given to the best singers."},{"bad":"The audience cheered loudly.","good":"The audience cheered loudly."},{"bad":"The final song write by a student.","good":"The final song was written by a student."},{"bad":"Everyone left with a smile.","good":"Everyone left with a smile."}]},
      {"bad":"The bakery prepared for the morning rush. The bread bake fresh every day. The smell reached the whole street. The first loaves sell before seven. The shop closes at noon on Sundays.","good":"The bakery prepared for the morning rush. The bread is baked fresh every day. The smell reached the whole street. The first loaves are sold before seven. The shop closes at noon on Sundays.","explanation":"Use \"is baked\" and \"are sold\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The bakery prepared for the morning rush.","good":"The bakery prepared for the morning rush."},{"bad":"The bread bake fresh every day.","good":"The bread is baked fresh every day."},{"bad":"The smell reached the whole street.","good":"The smell reached the whole street."},{"bad":"The first loaves sell before seven.","good":"The first loaves are sold before seven."},{"bad":"The shop closes at noon on Sundays.","good":"The shop closes at noon on Sundays."}]},
      {"bad":"The committee reviewed the new rules. The rules approve at last week's meeting. Staff received a written summary. The changes announce to everyone by email. The new rules start in June.","good":"The committee reviewed the new rules. The rules were approved at last week's meeting. Staff received a written summary. The changes were announced to everyone by email. The new rules start in June.","explanation":"Use \"were approved\" and \"were announced\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The committee reviewed the new rules.","good":"The committee reviewed the new rules."},{"bad":"The rules approve at last week's meeting.","good":"The rules were approved at last week's meeting."},{"bad":"Staff received a written summary.","good":"Staff received a written summary."},{"bad":"The changes announce to everyone by email.","good":"The changes were announced to everyone by email."},{"bad":"The new rules start in June.","good":"The new rules start in June."}]},
      {"bad":"The workers restored the old station. The roof repair after the winter storms. New windows fitted on the upper floor. The station reopened in the summer. The whole town was proud of the result.","good":"The workers restored the old station. The roof was repaired after the winter storms. New windows were fitted on the upper floor. The station reopened in the summer. The whole town was proud of the result.","explanation":"Use \"was repaired\" and \"were fitted\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The workers restored the old station.","good":"The workers restored the old station."},{"bad":"The roof repair after the winter storms.","good":"The roof was repaired after the winter storms."},{"bad":"New windows fitted on the upper floor.","good":"New windows were fitted on the upper floor."},{"bad":"The station reopened in the summer.","good":"The station reopened in the summer."},{"bad":"The whole town was proud of the result.","good":"The whole town was proud of the result."}]}
