    "6.5": [
      {"bad":"A strange noise woke the whole street. The accident was happened near the corner. Neighbours rushed outside at once. Nothing serious was occurred that night. Everyone returned to their homes.","good":"A strange noise woke the whole street. The accident happened near the corner. Neighbours rushed outside at once. Nothing serious occurred that night. Everyone returned to their homes.","explanation":"Intransitive verbs like \"happen\" and \"occur\" have no passive form.","sentences":[{"bad":"A strange noise woke the whole street.","good":"A strange noise woke the whole street."},{"bad":"The accident was happened near the corner.","good":"The accident happened near the corner."},{"bad":"Neighbours rushed outside at once.","good":"Neighbours rushed outside at once."},{"bad":"Nothing serious was occurred that night.","good":"Nothing serious occurred that night."},{"bad":"Everyone returned to their homes.","good":"Everyone returned to their homes."}]},
      {"bad":"The guests arrived late in the evening. A delay was occurred at the airport. The hosts kept the dinner warm. The flight was departed two hours late. The family welcomed them warmly.","good":"The guests arrived late in the evening. A delay occurred at the airport. The hosts kept the dinner warm. The flight departed two hours late. The family welcomed them warmly.","explanation":"\"Occur\" and \"depart\" cannot be used in the passive.","sentences":[{"bad":"The guests arrived late in the evening.","good":"The guests arrived late in the evening."},{"bad":"A delay was occurred at the airport.","good":"A delay occurred at the airport."},{"bad":"The hosts kept the dinner warm.","good":"The hosts kept the dinner warm."},{"bad":"The flight was departed two hours late.","good":"The flight departed two hours late."},{"bad":"The family welcomed them warmly.","good":"The family welcomed them warmly."}]},
      {"bad":"The festival brought visitors to the town. The main concert was lasted three hours. Musicians played on two stages. A large crowd was appeared by the river. The festival ended without trouble.","good":"The festival brought visitors to the town. The main concert lasted three hours. Musicians played on two stages. A large crowd appeared by the river. The festival ended without trouble.","explanation":"\"Last\" and \"appear\" cannot be used in the passive.","sentences":[{"bad":"The festival brought visitors to the town.","good":"The festival brought visitors to the town."},{"bad":"The main concert was lasted three hours.","good":"The main concert lasted three hours."},{"bad":"Musicians played on two stages.","good":"Musicians played on two stages."},{"bad":"A large crowd was appeared by the river.","good":"A large crowd appeared by the river."},{"bad":"The festival ended without trouble.","good":"The festival ended without trouble."}]},
      {"bad":"The hikers set off before sunrise. Their guide was risen with the sun. They followed a path through the pine woods. They were returned before dark. The trip was tiring but enjoyable.","good":"The hikers set off before sunrise. Their guide rose with the sun. They followed a path through the pine woods. They returned before dark. The trip was tiring but enjoyable.","explanation":"\"Rise\" and \"return\" cannot be used in the passive here; use the active forms.","sentences":[{"bad":"The hikers set off before sunrise.","good":"The hikers set off before sunrise."},{"bad":"Their guide was risen with the sun.","good":"Their guide rose with the sun."},{"bad":"They followed a path through the pine woods.","good":"They followed a path through the pine woods."},{"bad":"They were returned before dark.","good":"They returned before dark."},{"bad":"The trip was tiring but enjoyable.","good":"The trip was tiring but enjoyable."}]},
      {"bad":"The children waited for the school bus. The bus was arrived early that day. They climbed aboard quickly. Two late pupils was appeared at the corner. The bus left on time after all.","good":"The children waited for the school bus. The bus arrived early that day. They climbed aboard quickly. Two late pupils appeared at the corner. The bus left on time after all.","explanation":"\"Arrive\" and \"appear\" cannot be used in the passive.","sentences":[{"bad":"The children waited for the school bus.","good":"The children waited for the school bus."},{"bad":"The bus was arrived early that day.","good":"The bus arrived early that day."},{"bad":"They climbed aboard quickly.","good":"They climbed aboard quickly."},{"bad":"Two late pupils was appeared at the corner.","good":"Two late pupils appeared at the corner."},{"bad":"The bus left on time after all.","good":"The bus left on time after all."}]}
