    "6.6": [
      {"bad":"The students discussed the homework together. I am knowing the answer to the first question. My friend looked at the second one. She is believing it is too hard. In the end, we finished the whole exercise by dinner.","good":"The students discussed the homework together. I know the answer to the first question. My friend looked at the second one. She believes it is too hard. In the end, we finished the whole exercise by dinner.","explanation":"Stative verbs like \"know\" and \"believe\" are not used in the progressive.","sentences":[{"bad":"The students discussed the homework together.","good":"The students discussed the homework together."},{"bad":"I am knowing the answer to the first question.","good":"I know the answer to the first question."},{"bad":"My friend looked at the second one.","good":"My friend looked at the second one."},{"bad":"She is believing it is too hard.","good":"She believes it is too hard."},{"bad":"In the end, we finished the whole exercise by dinner.","good":"In the end, we finished the whole exercise by dinner."}]},
      {"bad":"The family settled in the new house. We are wanting a larger garden. The neighbours are very friendly. They are seeming happy to help us. We have settled in well.","good":"The family settled in the new house. We want a larger garden. The neighbours are very friendly. They seem happy to help us. We have settled in well.","explanation":"Use \"want\" and \"seem\", not \"are wanting\"/\"are seeming\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The family settled in the new house.","good":"The family settled in the new house."},{"bad":"We are wanting a larger garden.","good":"We want a larger garden."},{"bad":"The neighbours are very friendly.","good":"The neighbours are very friendly."},{"bad":"They are seeming happy to help us.","good":"They seem happy to help us."},{"bad":"We have settled in well.","good":"We have settled in well."}]},
      {"bad":"The customers admired the new display. I am preferring the blue scarf. My sister likes the red one better. She is understanding the price too well. We bought both in the end.","good":"The customers admired the new display. I prefer the blue scarf. My sister likes the red one better. She understands the price too well. We bought both in the end.","explanation":"Stative verbs \"prefer\" and \"understand\" stay in the simple present.","sentences":[{"bad":"The customers admired the new display.","good":"The customers admired the new display."},{"bad":"I am preferring the blue scarf.","good":"I prefer the blue scarf."},{"bad":"My sister likes the red one better.","good":"My sister likes the red one better."},{"bad":"She is understanding the price too well.","good":"She understands the price too well."},{"bad":"We bought both in the end.","good":"We bought both in the end."}]},
      {"bad":"The travellers reached the mountain village. We are hearing the church bells already. The air smells of pine and wood smoke. I am seeing the whole valley from here. The view was worth the long climb.","good":"The travellers reached the mountain village. We hear the church bells already. The air smells of pine and wood smoke. I see the whole valley from here. The view was worth the long climb.","explanation":"Verbs of perception like \"hear\" and \"see\" are stative here.","sentences":[{"bad":"The travellers reached the mountain village.","good":"The travellers reached the mountain village."},{"bad":"We are hearing the church bells already.","good":"We hear the church bells already."},{"bad":"The air smells of pine and wood smoke.","good":"The air smells of pine and wood smoke."},{"bad":"I am seeing the whole valley from here.","good":"I see the whole valley from here."},{"bad":"The view was worth the long climb.","good":"The view was worth the long climb."}]},
      {"bad":"The team reviewed the match on video. The coach is doubting the referee's decision. The players watched the replay closely. They are remembering the last goal clearly. They agreed to train harder.","good":"The team reviewed the match on video. The coach doubts the referee's decision. The players watched the replay closely. They remember the last goal clearly. They agreed to train harder.","explanation":"Use \"doubts\" and \"remember\", not the progressive forms.","sentences":[{"bad":"The team reviewed the match on video.","good":"The team reviewed the match on video."},{"bad":"The coach is doubting the referee's decision.","good":"The coach doubts the referee's decision."},{"bad":"The players watched the replay closely.","good":"The players watched the replay closely."},{"bad":"They are remembering the last goal clearly.","good":"They remember the last goal clearly."},{"bad":"They agreed to train harder.","good":"They agreed to train harder."}]}
