    "6.7": [
      {"bad":"My aunt told us a story from her childhood. She said she will visit the old town every summer. We listened with great interest. She explained that she is only ten at the time. The story made us all laugh.","good":"My aunt told us a story from her childhood. She said she would visit the old town every summer. We listened with great interest. She explained that she was only ten at the time. The story made us all laugh.","explanation":"In reported speech after a past verb, shift to the past: \"would visit\", \"was only ten\".","sentences":[{"bad":"My aunt told us a story from her childhood.","good":"My aunt told us a story from her childhood."},{"bad":"She said she will visit the old town every summer.","good":"She said she would visit the old town every summer."},{"bad":"We listened with great interest.","good":"We listened with great interest."},{"bad":"She explained that she is only ten at the time.","good":"She explained that she was only ten at the time."},{"bad":"The story made us all laugh.","good":"The story made us all laugh."}]},
      {"bad":"The manager described the new plan to the team. He said the changes will start next month. He explained the reason for each decision. He added that the budget increases by ten per cent. The team asked a few questions afterwards.","good":"The manager described the new plan to the team. He said the changes would start next month. He explained the reason for each decision. He added that the budget would increase by ten per cent. The team asked a few questions afterwards.","explanation":"Keep the tense consistent with the past reporting verb: \"would start\", \"would increase\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The manager described the new plan to the team.","good":"The manager described the new plan to the team."},{"bad":"He said the changes will start next month.","good":"He said the changes would start next month."},{"bad":"He explained the reason for each decision.","good":"He explained the reason for each decision."},{"bad":"He added that the budget increases by ten per cent.","good":"He added that the budget would increase by ten per cent."},{"bad":"The team asked a few questions afterwards.","good":"The team asked a few questions afterwards."}]},
      {"bad":"The pupil described her weekend to the class. She said she goes to the lake with her family. She showed a photo of the boat. She explained that the water was cold in the morning. Everyone wanted to visit the lake too.","good":"The pupil described her weekend to the class. She said she went to the lake with her family. She showed a photo of the boat. She explained that the water was cold in the morning. Everyone wanted to visit the lake too.","explanation":"After a past reporting verb, use \"went\", not \"goes\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The pupil described her weekend to the class.","good":"The pupil described her weekend to the class."},{"bad":"She said she goes to the lake with her family.","good":"She said she went to the lake with her family."},{"bad":"She showed a photo of the boat.","good":"She showed a photo of the boat."},{"bad":"She explained that the water was cold in the morning.","good":"She explained that the water was cold in the morning."},{"bad":"Everyone wanted to visit the lake too.","good":"Everyone wanted to visit the lake too."}]},
      {"bad":"The guide described the history of the castle. He said the castle is built in the fifteenth century. We walked around the old walls. He explained that the tower burns down long ago. The visit ended before the rain came.","good":"The guide described the history of the castle. He said the castle was built in the fifteenth century. We walked around the old walls. He explained that the tower had burned down long ago. The visit ended before the rain came.","explanation":"Shift to past or past perfect after the past reporting verb.","sentences":[{"bad":"The guide described the history of the castle.","good":"The guide described the history of the castle."},{"bad":"He said the castle is built in the fifteenth century.","good":"He said the castle was built in the fifteenth century."},{"bad":"We walked around the old walls.","good":"We walked around the old walls."},{"bad":"He explained that the tower burns down long ago.","good":"He explained that the tower had burned down long ago."},{"bad":"The visit ended before the rain came.","good":"The visit ended before the rain came."}]},
      {"bad":"The twins told their parents about the trip. They said the journey takes five hours. They described the mountain views. They said they will go again next year. Their parents were happy to hear it.","good":"The twins told their parents about the trip. They said the journey took five hours. They described the mountain views. They said they would go again next year. Their parents were happy to hear it.","explanation":"Use \"took\" and \"would go\" to match the past reporting verbs.","sentences":[{"bad":"The twins told their parents about the trip.","good":"The twins told their parents about the trip."},{"bad":"They said the journey takes five hours.","good":"They said the journey took five hours."},{"bad":"They described the mountain views.","good":"They described the mountain views."},{"bad":"They said they will go again next year.","good":"They said they would go again next year."},{"bad":"Their parents were happy to hear it.","good":"Their parents were happy to hear it."}]}
