      {"bad":"The team needs to improve its defence. The coach asked them to trains harder. They agreed to meet on Saturday. They promised to arrives early. The next match is on Friday.","good":"The team needs to improve its defence. The coach asked them to train harder. They agreed to meet on Saturday. They promised to arrive early. The next match is on Friday.","explanation":"Use \"to train\" and \"to arrive\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The team needs to improve its defence.","good":"The team needs to improve its defence."},{"bad":"The coach asked them to trains harder.","good":"The coach asked them to train harder."},{"bad":"They agreed to meet on Saturday.","good":"They agreed to meet on Saturday."},{"bad":"They promised to arrives early.","good":"They promised to arrive early."},{"bad":"The next match is on Friday.","good":"The next match is on Friday."}]},
      {"bad":"The school decided to build a new hall. The head teacher wanted to opens it in autumn. The builders started the work in June. They hoped to completes it before the term began. The hall opened right on time.","good":"The school decided to build a new hall. The head teacher wanted to open it in autumn. The builders started the work in June. They hoped to complete it before the term began. The hall opened right on time.","explanation":"Use the base form \"to open\" and \"to complete\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The school decided to build a new hall.","good":"The school decided to build a new hall."},{"bad":"The head teacher wanted to opens it in autumn.","good":"The head teacher wanted to open it in autumn."},{"bad":"The builders started the work in June.","good":"The builders started the work in June."},{"bad":"They hoped to completes it before the term began.","good":"They hoped to complete it before the term began."},{"bad":"The hall opened right on time.","good":"The hall opened right on time."}]},
      {"bad":"My neighbour offered to water our plants. She promised to takes care of them daily. We gave her a spare key. She was happy to helps us out. The plants looked healthy when we returned.","good":"My neighbour offered to water our plants. She promised to take care of them daily. We gave her a spare key. She was happy to help us out. The plants looked healthy when we returned.","explanation":"Use \"to take\" and \"to help\" after \"to\".","sentences":[{"bad":"My neighbour offered to water our plants.","good":"My neighbour offered to water our plants."},{"bad":"She promised to takes care of them daily.","good":"She promised to take care of them daily."},{"bad":"We gave her a spare key.","good":"We gave her a spare key."},{"bad":"She was happy to helps us out.","good":"She was happy to help us out."},{"bad":"The plants looked healthy when we returned.","good":"The plants looked healthy when we returned."}]}
