    "6.11": [
      {"bad":"The bin was full of old newspapers. Please take out it before the truck arrives. The truck comes on Thursday mornings. I will pick up them from the corner later. After that, the street is always tidy.","good":"The bin was full of old newspapers. Please take it out before the truck arrives. The truck comes on Thursday mornings. I will pick them up from the corner later. After that, the street is always tidy.","explanation":"A pronoun object goes between the verb and its particle: \"take it out\", \"pick them up\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The bin was full of old newspapers.","good":"The bin was full of old newspapers."},{"bad":"Please take out it before the truck arrives.","good":"Please take it out before the truck arrives."},{"bad":"The truck comes on Thursday mornings.","good":"The truck comes on Thursday mornings."},{"bad":"I will pick up them from the corner later.","good":"I will pick them up from the corner later."},{"bad":"After that, the street is always tidy.","good":"After that, the street is always tidy."}]},
      {"bad":"The room looked dark in the evening. Could you turn on it for me? The lamp stands by the armchair. Please switch off them before bed. We saved electricity that month.","good":"The room looked dark in the evening. Could you turn it on for me? The lamp stands by the armchair. Please switch them off before bed. We saved electricity that month.","explanation":"Use \"turn it on\" and \"switch them off\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The room looked dark in the evening.","good":"The room looked dark in the evening."},{"bad":"Could you turn on it for me?","good":"Could you turn it on for me?"},{"bad":"The lamp stands by the armchair.","good":"The lamp stands by the armchair."},{"bad":"Please switch off them before bed.","good":"Please switch them off before bed."},{"bad":"We saved electricity that month.","good":"We saved electricity that month."}]},
      {"bad":"My sister left her coat at school. She will look for it tomorrow. She asked the office for help. They promised to sort out it quickly. Eventually, the coat was found the next day.","good":"My sister left her coat at school. She will look for it tomorrow. She asked the office for help. They promised to sort it out quickly. Eventually, the coat was found the next day.","explanation":"The pronoun goes before the particle: \"sort it out\".","sentences":[{"bad":"My sister left her coat at school.","good":"My sister left her coat at school."},{"bad":"She will look for it tomorrow.","good":"She will look for it tomorrow."},{"bad":"She asked the office for help.","good":"She asked the office for help."},{"bad":"They promised to sort out it quickly.","good":"They promised to sort it out quickly."},{"bad":"Eventually, the coat was found the next day.","good":"Eventually, the coat was found the next day."}]},
      {"bad":"The guests arrived after dinner. We had to put up it in the spare room. The room was small but tidy. They helped us take down it in the morning. By noon, everything was back in place.","good":"The guests arrived after dinner. We had to put it up in the spare room. The room was small but tidy. They helped us take it down in the morning. By noon, everything was back in place.","explanation":"Use \"put it up\" and \"take it down\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The guests arrived after dinner.","good":"The guests arrived after dinner."},{"bad":"We had to put up it in the spare room.","good":"We had to put it up in the spare room."},{"bad":"The room was small but tidy.","good":"The room was small but tidy."},{"bad":"They helped us take down it in the morning.","good":"They helped us take it down in the morning."},{"bad":"By noon, everything was back in place.","good":"By noon, everything was back in place."}]},
      {"bad":"The class collected old toys for charity. They wanted to give away them to the shelter. A van arrived to collect the boxes. Volunteers helped load up them carefully. Afterwards, the shelter thanked the school warmly.","good":"The class collected old toys for charity. They wanted to give them away to the shelter. A van arrived to collect the boxes. Volunteers helped load them up carefully. Afterwards, the shelter thanked the school warmly.","explanation":"Use \"give them away\" and \"load them up\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The class collected old toys for charity.","good":"The class collected old toys for charity."},{"bad":"They wanted to give away them to the shelter.","good":"They wanted to give them away to the shelter."},{"bad":"A van arrived to collect the boxes.","good":"A van arrived to collect the boxes."},{"bad":"Volunteers helped load up them carefully.","good":"Volunteers helped load them up carefully."},{"bad":"Afterwards, the shelter thanked the school warmly.","good":"Afterwards, the shelter thanked the school warmly."}]}
