    "6.13": [
      {"bad":"The pupils finished the exercise early. Where you are going after school? Some of them go to the library. What she does read in the evenings? Then the bell rang for the end of the day.","good":"The pupils finished the exercise early. Where are you going after school? Some of them go to the library. What does she read in the evenings? Then the bell rang for the end of the day.","explanation":"In questions, invert subject and auxiliary: \"are you going\", \"does she read\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The pupils finished the exercise early.","good":"The pupils finished the exercise early."},{"bad":"Where you are going after school?","good":"Where are you going after school?"},{"bad":"Some of them go to the library.","good":"Some of them go to the library."},{"bad":"What she does read in the evenings?","good":"What does she read in the evenings?"},{"bad":"Then the bell rang for the end of the day.","good":"Then the bell rang for the end of the day."}]},
      {"bad":"The family planned a holiday abroad. When they will leave for the airport? The flight is early in the morning. Where you have put the tickets? Everything was ready on time.","good":"The family planned a holiday abroad. When will they leave for the airport? The flight is early in the morning. Where have you put the tickets? Everything was ready on time.","explanation":"Use \"will they leave\" and \"have you put\" in questions.","sentences":[{"bad":"The family planned a holiday abroad.","good":"The family planned a holiday abroad."},{"bad":"When they will leave for the airport?","good":"When will they leave for the airport?"},{"bad":"The flight is early in the morning.","good":"The flight is early in the morning."},{"bad":"Where you have put the tickets?","good":"Where have you put the tickets?"},{"bad":"Everything was ready on time.","good":"Everything was ready on time."}]},
      {"bad":"The chef prepared the evening menu. How you make the soup so quickly? The recipe is a family secret. Why she uses fresh herbs every time? The dinner was delicious.","good":"The chef prepared the evening menu. How do you make the soup so quickly? The recipe is a family secret. Why does she use fresh herbs every time? The dinner was delicious.","explanation":"Questions need \"do/does\": \"do you make\", \"does she use\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The chef prepared the evening menu.","good":"The chef prepared the evening menu."},{"bad":"How you make the soup so quickly?","good":"How do you make the soup so quickly?"},{"bad":"The recipe is a family secret.","good":"The recipe is a family secret."},{"bad":"Why she uses fresh herbs every time?","good":"Why does she use fresh herbs every time?"},{"bad":"The dinner was delicious.","good":"The dinner was delicious."}]},
      {"bad":"The team travelled to the away match. When the coach will announce the line-up? The players waited in the changing room. Who you saw at the stadium yesterday? The match began at three.","good":"The team travelled to the away match. When will the coach announce the line-up? The players waited in the changing room. Who did you see at the stadium yesterday? The match began at three.","explanation":"Use \"will the coach announce\" and \"did you see\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The team travelled to the away match.","good":"The team travelled to the away match."},{"bad":"When the coach will announce the line-up?","good":"When will the coach announce the line-up?"},{"bad":"The players waited in the changing room.","good":"The players waited in the changing room."},{"bad":"Who you saw at the stadium yesterday?","good":"Who did you see at the stadium yesterday?"},{"bad":"The match began at three.","good":"The match began at three."}]},
      {"bad":"The students organised a charity run. Where they will start the race? The route goes through the park. How long it will take to finish? In the end, the event raised a lot of money.","good":"The students organised a charity run. Where will they start the race? The route goes through the park. How long will it take to finish? In the end, the event raised a lot of money.","explanation":"Invert the auxiliary: \"will they start\", \"will it take\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The students organised a charity run.","good":"The students organised a charity run."},{"bad":"Where they will start the race?","good":"Where will they start the race?"},{"bad":"The route goes through the park.","good":"The route goes through the park."},{"bad":"How long it will take to finish?","good":"How long will it take to finish?"},{"bad":"In the end, the event raised a lot of money.","good":"In the end, the event raised a lot of money."}]}
