    "7.2": [
      {"bad":"The two sisters both love running. Anna is more taller than her sister. She trains three times a week. Her times are getting more better every month. The coach expects a strong season.","good":"The two sisters both love running. Anna is taller than her sister. She trains three times a week. Her times are getting better every month. The coach expects a strong season.","explanation":"Use only one comparative marker: \"taller\", \"better\" (never \"more taller\").","sentences":[{"bad":"The two sisters both love running.","good":"The two sisters both love running."},{"bad":"Anna is more taller than her sister.","good":"Anna is taller than her sister."},{"bad":"She trains three times a week.","good":"She trains three times a week."},{"bad":"Her times are getting more better every month.","good":"Her times are getting better every month."},{"bad":"The coach expects a strong season.","good":"The coach expects a strong season."}]},
      {"bad":"The city has two main bridges. The new bridge is more wider than the old one. It carries traffic in both directions. The old bridge is more narrower. Both bridges are busy at rush hour.","good":"The city has two main bridges. The new bridge is wider than the old one. It carries traffic in both directions. The old bridge is narrower. Both bridges are busy at rush hour.","explanation":"Use \"wider\" and \"narrower\", not \"more wider\"/\"more narrower\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The city has two main bridges.","good":"The city has two main bridges."},{"bad":"The new bridge is more wider than the old one.","good":"The new bridge is wider than the old one."},{"bad":"It carries traffic in both directions.","good":"It carries traffic in both directions."},{"bad":"The old bridge is more narrower.","good":"The old bridge is narrower."},{"bad":"Both bridges are busy at rush hour.","good":"Both bridges are busy at rush hour."}]},
