    "7.3": [
      {"bad":"The class studied mountains around the world. Everest is the most highest mountain on Earth. Many climbers dream of reaching it. It is also the most famousest peak in the world. The subject fascinated everyone.","good":"The class studied mountains around the world. Everest is the highest mountain on Earth. Many climbers dream of reaching it. It is also the most famous peak in the world. The subject fascinated everyone.","explanation":"Use one superlative marker: \"the highest\", \"the most famous\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The class studied mountains around the world.","good":"The class studied mountains around the world."},{"bad":"Everest is the most highest mountain on Earth.","good":"Everest is the highest mountain on Earth."},{"bad":"Many climbers dream of reaching it.","good":"Many climbers dream of reaching it."},{"bad":"It is also the most famousest peak in the world.","good":"It is also the most famous peak in the world."},{"bad":"The subject fascinated everyone.","good":"The subject fascinated everyone."}]},
      {"bad":"The library holds thousands of books. This is the most oldest one in the collection. It was printed two hundred years ago. It is the most rarest book here. Visitors come to see it every week.","good":"The library holds thousands of books. This is the oldest one in the collection. It was printed two hundred years ago. It is the rarest book here. Visitors come to see it every week.","explanation":"Use \"the oldest\" and \"the rarest\" (no \"most\" with -est).","sentences":[{"bad":"The library holds thousands of books.","good":"The library holds thousands of books."},{"bad":"This is the most oldest one in the collection.","good":"This is the oldest one in the collection."},{"bad":"It was printed two hundred years ago.","good":"It was printed two hundred years ago."},{"bad":"It is the most rarest book here.","good":"It is the rarest book here."},{"bad":"Visitors come to see it every week.","good":"Visitors come to see it every week."}]},
      {"bad":"We watched a documentary about oceans. The Pacific is the most deepest ocean. It covers a huge area of the planet. It is also the most largest by far. The film was full of surprises.","good":"We watched a documentary about oceans. The Pacific is the deepest ocean. It covers a huge area of the planet. It is also the largest by far. The film was full of surprises.","explanation":"Use \"the deepest\" and \"the largest\" as single superlatives.","sentences":[{"bad":"We watched a documentary about oceans.","good":"We watched a documentary about oceans."},{"bad":"The Pacific is the most deepest ocean.","good":"The Pacific is the deepest ocean."},{"bad":"It covers a huge area of the planet.","good":"It covers a huge area of the planet."},{"bad":"It is also the most largest by far.","good":"It is also the largest by far."},{"bad":"The film was full of surprises.","good":"The film was full of surprises."}]},
      {"bad":"The bakery is famous in our town. Customers say it makes the most best bread. The baker starts work at four. She uses the most freshest flour. There is always a queue by eight.","good":"The bakery is famous in our town. Customers say it makes the best bread. The baker starts work at four. She uses the freshest flour. There is always a queue by eight.","explanation":"Use \"the best\" and \"the freshest\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The bakery is famous in our town.","good":"The bakery is famous in our town."},{"bad":"Customers say it makes the most best bread.","good":"Customers say it makes the best bread."},{"bad":"The baker starts work at four.","good":"The baker starts work at four."},{"bad":"She uses the most freshest flour.","good":"She uses the freshest flour."},{"bad":"There is always a queue by eight.","good":"There is always a queue by eight."}]},
      {"bad":"The team reviewed its season. That was the most worst match of the year. They lost by four goals. It was also the most unluckiest day. They improved in every game after that.","good":"The team reviewed its season. That was the worst match of the year. They lost by four goals. It was also the unluckiest day. They improved in every game after that.","explanation":"Use \"the worst\" and \"the unluckiest\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The team reviewed its season.","good":"The team reviewed its season."},{"bad":"That was the most worst match of the year.","good":"That was the worst match of the year."},{"bad":"They lost by four goals.","good":"They lost by four goals."},{"bad":"It was also the most unluckiest day.","good":"It was also the unluckiest day."},{"bad":"They improved in every game after that.","good":"They improved in every game after that."}]}
