    "7.4": [
      {"bad":"The twins went to the same school. Tom is as tall than his brother. People often confuse them. They are not so different than they look. Their teachers tell them apart easily.","good":"The twins went to the same school. Tom is as tall as his brother. People often confuse them. They are not so different as they look. Their teachers tell them apart easily.","explanation":"Use \"as ... as\" in comparisons of equality, and \"not so ... as\" in the negative.","sentences":[{"bad":"The twins went to the same school.","good":"The twins went to the same school."},{"bad":"Tom is as tall than his brother.","good":"Tom is as tall as his brother."},{"bad":"People often confuse them.","good":"People often confuse them."},{"bad":"They are not so different than they look.","good":"They are not so different as they look."},{"bad":"Their teachers tell them apart easily.","good":"Their teachers tell them apart easily."}]},
      {"bad":"The two cafés sit on the same street. The new café is not as busy than the old one. It opened just last month. Its coffee is as good than the other's. More customers discover it each week.","good":"The two cafés sit on the same street. The new café is not as busy as the old one. It opened just last month. Its coffee is as good as the other's. More customers discover it each week.","explanation":"Use \"as busy as\" and \"as good as\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The two cafés sit on the same street.","good":"The two cafés sit on the same street."},{"bad":"The new café is not as busy than the old one.","good":"The new café is not as busy as the old one."},{"bad":"It opened just last month.","good":"It opened just last month."},{"bad":"Its coffee is as good than the other's.","good":"Its coffee is as good as the other's."},{"bad":"More customers discover it each week.","good":"More customers discover it each week."}]},
      {"bad":"The siblings both play the piano. Maya practises as often than her brother. They perform at the same concert. Her playing is not so confident than his yet. They support each other well.","good":"The siblings both play the piano. Maya practises as often as her brother. They perform at the same concert. Her playing is not so confident as his yet. They support each other well.","explanation":"Use \"as often as\" and \"not so ... as\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The siblings both play the piano.","good":"The siblings both play the piano."},{"bad":"Maya practises as often than her brother.","good":"Maya practises as often as her brother."},{"bad":"They perform at the same concert.","good":"They perform at the same concert."},{"bad":"Her playing is not so confident than his yet.","good":"Her playing is not so confident as his yet."},{"bad":"They support each other well.","good":"They support each other well."}]},
      {"bad":"The hikers compared two routes. The north path is not as steep than the south one. But it is twice as long. Both views are as beautiful than any painting. They chose the shorter route.","good":"The hikers compared two routes. The north path is not as steep as the south one. But it is twice as long. Both views are as beautiful as any painting. They chose the shorter route.","explanation":"Use \"as steep as\" and \"as beautiful as\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The hikers compared two routes.","good":"The hikers compared two routes."},{"bad":"The north path is not as steep than the south one.","good":"The north path is not as steep as the south one."},{"bad":"But it is twice as long.","good":"But it is twice as long."},{"bad":"Both views are as beautiful than any painting.","good":"Both views are as beautiful as any painting."},{"bad":"They chose the shorter route.","good":"They chose the shorter route."}]},
      {"bad":"The competition featured two strong teams. The visitors were as quick than the home side. The match stayed level for an hour. The home players were not so tired than the visitors. The home team scored late on.","good":"The competition featured two strong teams. The visitors were as quick as the home side. The match stayed level for an hour. The home players were not so tired as the visitors. The home team scored late on.","explanation":"Use \"as quick as\" and \"not so ... as\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The competition featured two strong teams.","good":"The competition featured two strong teams."},{"bad":"The visitors were as quick than the home side.","good":"The visitors were as quick as the home side."},{"bad":"The match stayed level for an hour.","good":"The match stayed level for an hour."},{"bad":"The home players were not so tired than the visitors.","good":"The home players were not so tired as the visitors."},{"bad":"The home team scored late on.","good":"The home team scored late on."}]}
