    "7.5": [
      {"bad":"The choir performed at the school concert. The soloist sang beautiful. The audience clapped for a long time. The pianist played the final piece very good. Everyone left in high spirits.","good":"The choir performed at the school concert. The soloist sang beautifully. The audience clapped for a long time. The pianist played the final piece very well. Everyone left in high spirits.","explanation":"Modify a verb with an adverb: \"sang beautifully\", \"played ... well\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The choir performed at the school concert.","good":"The choir performed at the school concert."},{"bad":"The soloist sang beautiful.","good":"The soloist sang beautifully."},{"bad":"The audience clapped for a long time.","good":"The audience clapped for a long time."},{"bad":"The pianist played the final piece very good.","good":"The pianist played the final piece very well."},{"bad":"Everyone left in high spirits.","good":"Everyone left in high spirits."}]},
      {"bad":"The driver took the mountain road carefully. He always drives very careful. The road winds through the hills. He checks his mirrors regular. They reached the coast safely.","good":"The driver took the mountain road carefully. He always drives very carefully. The road winds through the hills. He checks his mirrors regularly. They reached the coast safely.","explanation":"Use the adverbs \"carefully\" and \"regularly\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The driver took the mountain road carefully.","good":"The driver took the mountain road carefully."},{"bad":"He always drives very careful.","good":"He always drives very carefully."},{"bad":"The road winds through the hills.","good":"The road winds through the hills."},{"bad":"He checks his mirrors regular.","good":"He checks his mirrors regularly."},{"bad":"They reached the coast safely.","good":"They reached the coast safely."}]},
      {"bad":"The pupil answered the questions quickly. She writes very neat. The teacher praised her work. She also listens very attentive. Her marks improved all year.","good":"The pupil answered the questions quickly. She writes very neatly. The teacher praised her work. She also listens very attentively. Her marks improved all year.","explanation":"Use \"neatly\" and \"attentively\" to modify the verbs.","sentences":[{"bad":"The pupil answered the questions quickly.","good":"The pupil answered the questions quickly."},{"bad":"She writes very neat.","good":"She writes very neatly."},{"bad":"The teacher praised her work.","good":"The teacher praised her work."},{"bad":"She also listens very attentive.","good":"She also listens very attentively."},{"bad":"Her marks improved all year.","good":"Her marks improved all year."}]},
      {"bad":"The team prepared for the final. They trained very hard and played brilliant. The crowd cheered throughout. The captain spoke calm to the players. They lifted the trophy at last.","good":"The team prepared for the final. They trained very hard and played brilliantly. The crowd cheered throughout. The captain spoke calmly to the players. They lifted the trophy at last.","explanation":"Use \"brilliantly\" and \"calmly\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The team prepared for the final.","good":"The team prepared for the final."},{"bad":"They trained very hard and played brilliant.","good":"They trained very hard and played brilliantly."},{"bad":"The crowd cheered throughout.","good":"The crowd cheered throughout."},{"bad":"The captain spoke calm to the players.","good":"The captain spoke calmly to the players."},{"bad":"They lifted the trophy at last.","good":"They lifted the trophy at last."}]},
      {"bad":"The chef prepared the evening meal. She chopped the vegetables quick and precise. The sauce simmered on the stove. She tasted it careful before serving. The guests enjoyed every course.","good":"The chef prepared the evening meal. She chopped the vegetables quickly and precisely. The sauce simmered on the stove. She tasted it carefully before serving. The guests enjoyed every course.","explanation":"Use \"quickly\", \"precisely\", and \"carefully\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The chef prepared the evening meal.","good":"The chef prepared the evening meal."},{"bad":"She chopped the vegetables quick and precise.","good":"She chopped the vegetables quickly and precisely."},{"bad":"The sauce simmered on the stove.","good":"The sauce simmered on the stove."},{"bad":"She tasted it careful before serving.","good":"She tasted it carefully before serving."},{"bad":"The guests enjoyed every course.","good":"The guests enjoyed every course."}]}
