      {"bad":"My aunt married young. She is married with a teacher. They live in the next town. She has been married to him for ten years. They are a happy couple.","good":"My aunt married young. She is married to a teacher. They live in the next town. She has been married to him for ten years. They are a happy couple.","explanation":"Use \"married to\" for people.","sentences":[{"bad":"My aunt married young.","good":"My aunt married young."},{"bad":"She is married with a teacher.","good":"She is married to a teacher."},{"bad":"They live in the next town.","good":"They live in the next town."},{"bad":"She has been married to him for ten years.","good":"She has been married to him for ten years."},{"bad":"They are a happy couple.","good":"They are a happy couple."}]},
      {"bad":"The success of the plan is unsure. Everything depends of the weather. We will decide on Friday. Our plans depend of the forecast. We hope for a clear day.","good":"The success of the plan is unsure. Everything depends on the weather. We will decide on Friday. Our plans depend on the forecast. We hope for a clear day.","explanation":"Use \"depend on\", never \"depend of\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The success of the plan is unsure.","good":"The success of the plan is unsure."},{"bad":"Everything depends of the weather.","good":"Everything depends on the weather."},{"bad":"We will decide on Friday.","good":"We will decide on Friday."},{"bad":"Our plans depend of the forecast.","good":"Our plans depend on the forecast."},{"bad":"We hope for a clear day.","good":"We hope for a clear day."}]},
      {"bad":"The doctor gave clear advice. This medicine is good to a headache. Take it twice a day. It is also useful to a sore throat. The chemist explained the dose.","good":"The doctor gave clear advice. This medicine is good for a headache. Take it twice a day. It is also useful for a sore throat. The chemist explained the dose.","explanation":"Use \"good for\" and \"useful for\" a purpose or condition.","sentences":[{"bad":"The doctor gave clear advice.","good":"The doctor gave clear advice."},{"bad":"This medicine is good to a headache.","good":"This medicine is good for a headache."},{"bad":"Take it twice a day.","good":"Take it twice a day."},{"bad":"It is also useful to a sore throat.","good":"It is also useful for a sore throat."},{"bad":"The chemist explained the dose.","good":"The chemist explained the dose."}]},
      {"bad":"The town is proud of its bridge. The bridge is made by steel and stone. It was built by local workers. The design was made of a young engineer. The bridge still stands today.","good":"The town is proud of its bridge. The bridge is made of steel and stone. It was built by local workers. The design was made by a young engineer. The bridge still stands today.","explanation":"Use \"made of\" for material and \"made by\" for the maker.","sentences":[{"bad":"The town is proud of its bridge.","good":"The town is proud of its bridge."},{"bad":"The bridge is made by steel and stone.","good":"The bridge is made of steel and stone."},{"bad":"It was built by local workers.","good":"It was built by local workers."},{"bad":"The design was made of a young engineer.","good":"The design was made by a young engineer."},{"bad":"The bridge still stands today.","good":"The bridge still stands today."}]},
      {"bad":"The teacher thanked the class. She was very pleased of their work. The results were excellent. She was proud of their effort. The class felt encouraged.","good":"The teacher thanked the class. She was very pleased with their work. The results were excellent. She was proud of their effort. The class felt encouraged.","explanation":"Use \"pleased with\" and \"proud of\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The teacher thanked the class.","good":"The teacher thanked the class."},{"bad":"She was very pleased of their work.","good":"She was very pleased with their work."},{"bad":"The results were excellent.","good":"The results were excellent."},{"bad":"She was proud of their effort.","good":"She was proud of their effort."},{"bad":"The class felt encouraged.","good":"The class felt encouraged."}]}
