    "8.3": [
      {"bad":"The guests reached the hotel late. They arrived to the city after midnight. A taxi waited at the entrance. It took them straight at the hotel. They were asleep within an hour.","good":"The guests reached the hotel late. They arrived in the city after midnight. A taxi waited at the entrance. It took them straight to the hotel. They were asleep within an hour.","explanation":"Use \"arrive in\" a city and \"to\" for a destination with \"take\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The guests reached the hotel late.","good":"The guests reached the hotel late."},{"bad":"They arrived to the city after midnight.","good":"They arrived in the city after midnight."},{"bad":"A taxi waited at the entrance.","good":"A taxi waited at the entrance."},{"bad":"It took them straight at the hotel.","good":"It took them straight to the hotel."},{"bad":"They were asleep within an hour.","good":"They were asleep within an hour."}]},
      {"bad":"My brother loves music. He listens music every evening. He plays the guitar too. He listens to the radio at breakfast. He dreams of joining a band.","good":"My brother loves music. He listens to music every evening. He plays the guitar too. He listens to the radio at breakfast. He dreams of joining a band.","explanation":"Use \"listen to\" with an object.","sentences":[{"bad":"My brother loves music.","good":"My brother loves music."},{"bad":"He listens music every evening.","good":"He listens to music every evening."},{"bad":"He plays the guitar too.","good":"He plays the guitar too."},{"bad":"He listens to the radio at breakfast.","good":"He listens to the radio at breakfast."},{"bad":"He dreams of joining a band.","good":"He dreams of joining a band."}]},
      {"bad":"The students prepared for the test. They were waiting the results nervously. The teacher marked the papers quickly. They asked the teacher about their marks. The results were good.","good":"The students prepared for the test. They were waiting for the results nervously. The teacher marked the papers quickly. They asked the teacher about their marks. The results were good.","explanation":"Use \"wait for\" with an object.","sentences":[{"bad":"The students prepared for the test.","good":"The students prepared for the test."},{"bad":"They were waiting the results nervously.","good":"They were waiting for the results nervously."},{"bad":"The teacher marked the papers quickly.","good":"The teacher marked the papers quickly."},{"bad":"They asked the teacher about their marks.","good":"They asked the teacher about their marks."},{"bad":"The results were good.","good":"The results were good."}]},
      {"bad":"The family moved to a new town. They had to look after of the garden. The house came with a large lawn. They also took care of the old trees. The garden soon looked lovely.","good":"The family moved to a new town. They had to look after the garden. The house came with a large lawn. They also took care of the old trees. The garden soon looked lovely.","explanation":"\"Look after\" and \"take care of\" take objects without extra prepositions.","sentences":[{"bad":"The family moved to a new town.","good":"The family moved to a new town."},{"bad":"They had to look after of the garden.","good":"They had to look after the garden."},{"bad":"The house came with a large lawn.","good":"The house came with a large lawn."},{"bad":"They also took care of the old trees.","good":"They also took care of the old trees."},{"bad":"The garden soon looked lovely.","good":"The garden soon looked lovely."}]},
      {"bad":"The manager reviewed the report. She was responsible of the whole team. She trained the new staff. She was also in charge for the schedule. The team met every Monday.","good":"The manager reviewed the report. She was responsible for the whole team. She trained the new staff. She was also in charge of the schedule. The team met every Monday.","explanation":"Use \"responsible for\" and \"in charge of\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The manager reviewed the report.","good":"The manager reviewed the report."},{"bad":"She was responsible of the whole team.","good":"She was responsible for the whole team."},{"bad":"She trained the new staff.","good":"She trained the new staff."},{"bad":"She was also in charge for the schedule.","good":"She was also in charge of the schedule."},{"bad":"The team met every Monday.","good":"The team met every Monday."}]}
