    "9.2": [
      {"bad":"The kitchen was busy that morning. The box of apples are on the table. The recipe card sits beside it. A bowl of onions wait to be chopped. The cook works quickly.","good":"The kitchen was busy that morning. The box of apples is on the table. The recipe card sits beside it. A bowl of onions waits to be chopped. The cook works quickly.","explanation":"The verb agrees with the head noun (\"box\", \"bowl\"), not the phrase after \"of\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The kitchen was busy that morning.","good":"The kitchen was busy that morning."},{"bad":"The box of apples are on the table.","good":"The box of apples is on the table."},{"bad":"The recipe card sits beside it.","good":"The recipe card sits beside it."},{"bad":"A bowl of onions wait to be chopped.","good":"A bowl of onions waits to be chopped."},{"bad":"The cook works quickly.","good":"The cook works quickly."}]},
      {"bad":"The office prepared for the audit. The manager, along with the staff, are ready. The files are neatly arranged. A folder of receipts sit on the desk. Everything is in order.","good":"The office prepared for the audit. The manager, along with the staff, is ready. The files are neatly arranged. A folder of receipts sits on the desk. Everything is in order.","explanation":"Ignore the interrupting phrase: \"the manager ... is\", \"a folder ... sits\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The office prepared for the audit.","good":"The office prepared for the audit."},{"bad":"The manager, along with the staff, are ready.","good":"The manager, along with the staff, is ready."},{"bad":"The files are neatly arranged.","good":"The files are neatly arranged."},{"bad":"A folder of receipts sit on the desk.","good":"A folder of receipts sits on the desk."},{"bad":"Everything is in order.","good":"Everything is in order."}]},
      {"bad":"The choir gave a fine performance. The group of singers were in good voice. The audience applauded warmly. A pair of soloists shine in the second half. The concert ended on a high note.","good":"The choir gave a fine performance. The group of singers was in good voice. The audience applauded warmly. A pair of soloists shines in the second half. The concert ended on a high note.","explanation":"The subject is \"group\"/\"pair\", so use \"was\" and \"shines\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The choir gave a fine performance.","good":"The choir gave a fine performance."},{"bad":"The group of singers were in good voice.","good":"The group of singers was in good voice."},{"bad":"The audience applauded warmly.","good":"The audience applauded warmly."},{"bad":"A pair of soloists shine in the second half.","good":"A pair of soloists shines in the second half."},{"bad":"The concert ended on a high note.","good":"The concert ended on a high note."}]},
      {"bad":"The team travelled by coach. The captain, as well as the players, were cheerful. They sang songs for the whole trip. A crowd of fans wait at the stadium. The match began in bright sunshine.","good":"The team travelled by coach. The captain, as well as the players, was cheerful. They sang songs for the whole trip. A crowd of fans waits at the stadium. The match began in bright sunshine.","explanation":"Use the head noun: \"the captain ... was\", \"a crowd ... waits\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The team travelled by coach.","good":"The team travelled by coach."},{"bad":"The captain, as well as the players, were cheerful.","good":"The captain, as well as the players, was cheerful."},{"bad":"They sang songs for the whole trip.","good":"They sang songs for the whole trip."},{"bad":"A crowd of fans wait at the stadium.","good":"A crowd of fans waits at the stadium."},{"bad":"The match began in bright sunshine.","good":"The match began in bright sunshine."}]},
      {"bad":"The museum opened a new wing. The collection of paintings draw large crowds. Visitors queue at the entrance. The curator, together with the team, are delighted. The new wing is a great success.","good":"The museum opened a new wing. The collection of paintings draws large crowds. Visitors queue at the entrance. The curator, together with the team, is delighted. The new wing is a great success.","explanation":"Agreement follows \"collection\" and \"curator\": \"draws\", \"is\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The museum opened a new wing.","good":"The museum opened a new wing."},{"bad":"The collection of paintings draw large crowds.","good":"The collection of paintings draws large crowds."},{"bad":"Visitors queue at the entrance.","good":"Visitors queue at the entrance."},{"bad":"The curator, together with the team, are delighted.","good":"The curator, together with the team, is delighted."},{"bad":"The new wing is a great success.","good":"The new wing is a great success."}]}
