      {"bad":"The children were excited. Since it was raining, so they stayed inside. They built a den with cushions. Even though they were indoors, but they had fun. The afternoon passed quickly.","good":"The children were excited. Since it was raining, they stayed inside. They built a den with cushions. Even though they were indoors, they had fun. The afternoon passed quickly.","explanation":"Use one subordinator only: \"since ... they\", \"even though ... they\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The children were excited.","good":"The children were excited."},{"bad":"Since it was raining, so they stayed inside.","good":"Since it was raining, they stayed inside."},{"bad":"They built a den with cushions.","good":"They built a den with cushions."},{"bad":"Even though they were indoors, but they had fun.","good":"Even though they were indoors, they had fun."},{"bad":"The afternoon passed quickly.","good":"The afternoon passed quickly."}]},
      {"bad":"The bus was crowded. Although the seats were full, but we stood near the door. The journey was short. Because the traffic was light, so we arrived early. We caught the next bus home.","good":"The bus was crowded. Although the seats were full, we stood near the door. The journey was short. Because the traffic was light, we arrived early. We caught the next bus home.","explanation":"Avoid the double connector \"although ... but\" and \"because ... so\".","sentences":[{"bad":"The bus was crowded.","good":"The bus was crowded."},{"bad":"Although the seats were full, but we stood near the door.","good":"Although the seats were full, we stood near the door."},{"bad":"The journey was short.","good":"The journey was short."},{"bad":"Because the traffic was light, so we arrived early.","good":"Because the traffic was light, we arrived early."},{"bad":"We caught the next bus home.","good":"We caught the next bus home."}]},
      {"bad":"The exam was difficult. Even though she had studied, but she felt nervous. She read each question twice. As the clock ticked, so she worked faster. She passed with a good mark.","good":"The exam was difficult. Even though she had studied, she felt nervous. She read each question twice. As the clock ticked, she worked faster. She passed with a good mark.","explanation":"Use a single subordinating conjunction.","sentences":[{"bad":"The exam was difficult.","good":"The exam was difficult."},{"bad":"Even though she had studied, but she felt nervous.","good":"Even though she had studied, she felt nervous."},{"bad":"She read each question twice.","good":"She read each question twice."},{"bad":"As the clock ticked, so she worked faster.","good":"As the clock ticked, she worked faster."},{"bad":"She passed with a good mark.","good":"She passed with a good mark."}]},
      {"bad":"The garden was overgrown. Although nobody had time, but the neighbours helped. They cleared it in a weekend. Since the weather was fine, so they worked outside. The garden looked lovely again.","good":"The garden was overgrown. Although nobody had time, the neighbours helped. They cleared it in a weekend. Since the weather was fine, they worked outside. The garden looked lovely again.","explanation":"Drop the extra \"but\"/\"so\" after a subordinator.","sentences":[{"bad":"The garden was overgrown.","good":"The garden was overgrown."},{"bad":"Although nobody had time, but the neighbours helped.","good":"Although nobody had time, the neighbours helped."},{"bad":"They cleared it in a weekend.","good":"They cleared it in a weekend."},{"bad":"Since the weather was fine, so they worked outside.","good":"Since the weather was fine, they worked outside."},{"bad":"The garden looked lovely again.","good":"The garden looked lovely again."}]}
