      {"bad":"The pupils worked quietly. When the bell rang they packed away. The teacher dismissed the class. Before lunch they finished the exercise. The afternoon lesson began at one.","good":"The pupils worked quietly. When the bell rang, they packed away. The teacher dismissed the class. Before lunch, they finished the exercise. The afternoon lesson began at one.","explanation":"A comma follows an introductory clause.","sentences":[{"bad":"The pupils worked quietly.","good":"The pupils worked quietly."},{"bad":"When the bell rang they packed away.","good":"When the bell rang, they packed away."},{"bad":"The teacher dismissed the class.","good":"The teacher dismissed the class."},{"bad":"Before lunch they finished the exercise.","good":"Before lunch, they finished the exercise."},{"bad":"The afternoon lesson began at one.","good":"The afternoon lesson began at one."}]},
      {"bad":"The train pulled out of the station. As the sun rose the mist cleared. The countryside looked fresh. Along the river we saw herons. The journey passed pleasantly.","good":"The train pulled out of the station. As the sun rose, the mist cleared. The countryside looked fresh. Along the river, we saw herons. The journey passed pleasantly.","explanation":"Set off the opening clause with a comma.","sentences":[{"bad":"The train pulled out of the station.","good":"The train pulled out of the station."},{"bad":"As the sun rose the mist cleared.","good":"As the sun rose, the mist cleared."},{"bad":"The countryside looked fresh.","good":"The countryside looked fresh."},{"bad":"Along the river we saw herons.","good":"Along the river, we saw herons."},{"bad":"The journey passed pleasantly.","good":"The journey passed pleasantly."}]},
      {"bad":"The choir gathered on the stage. After a short break they sang again. The audience listened in silence. In the second half the tempo quickened. The concert ended to applause.","good":"The choir gathered on the stage. After a short break, they sang again. The audience listened in silence. In the second half, the tempo quickened. The concert ended to applause.","explanation":"Use a comma after the introductory phrase.","sentences":[{"bad":"The choir gathered on the stage.","good":"The choir gathered on the stage."},{"bad":"After a short break they sang again.","good":"After a short break, they sang again."},{"bad":"The audience listened in silence.","good":"The audience listened in silence."},{"bad":"In the second half the tempo quickened.","good":"In the second half, the tempo quickened."},{"bad":"The concert ended to applause.","good":"The concert ended to applause."}]},
      {"bad":"The gardener started early. Before the rain came she finished planting. The soil was soft and dark. By noon the whole bed was done. The garden looked full of promise.","good":"The gardener started early. Before the rain came, she finished planting. The soil was soft and dark. By noon, the whole bed was done. The garden looked full of promise.","explanation":"Introductory phrases are followed by a comma.","sentences":[{"bad":"The gardener started early.","good":"The gardener started early."},{"bad":"Before the rain came she finished planting.","good":"Before the rain came, she finished planting."},{"bad":"The soil was soft and dark.","good":"The soil was soft and dark."},{"bad":"By noon the whole bed was done.","good":"By noon, the whole bed was done."},{"bad":"The garden looked full of promise.","good":"The garden looked full of promise."}]}
