    "10.4": [
      {"bad":"My father works at the hospital. My father who is a doctor loves golf. He plays every Sunday. His friend who works with him joins too. They enjoy the fresh air.","good":"My father works at the hospital. My father, who is a doctor, loves golf. He plays every Sunday. His friend, who works with him, joins too. They enjoy the fresh air.","explanation":"A non-restrictive relative clause (extra information) is set off with commas.","sentences":[{"bad":"My father works at the hospital.","good":"My father works at the hospital."},{"bad":"My father who is a doctor loves golf.","good":"My father, who is a doctor, loves golf."},{"bad":"He plays every Sunday.","good":"He plays every Sunday."},{"bad":"His friend who works with him joins too.","good":"His friend, who works with him, joins too."},{"bad":"They enjoy the fresh air.","good":"They enjoy the fresh air."}]},
      {"bad":"The town has an old castle. The castle which is on a hill attracts tourists. It was built centuries ago. The tower which is the tallest part offers a view. Visitors climb it on sunny days.","good":"The town has an old castle. The castle, which is on a hill, attracts tourists. It was built centuries ago. The tower, which is the tallest part, offers a view. Visitors climb it on sunny days.","explanation":"Set off the non-essential clause with commas.","sentences":[{"bad":"The town has an old castle.","good":"The town has an old castle."},{"bad":"The castle which is on a hill attracts tourists.","good":"The castle, which is on a hill, attracts tourists."},{"bad":"It was built centuries ago.","good":"It was built centuries ago."},{"bad":"The tower which is the tallest part offers a view.","good":"The tower, which is the tallest part, offers a view."},{"bad":"Visitors climb it on sunny days.","good":"Visitors climb it on sunny days."}]},
      {"bad":"Our neighbour owns a small boat. His boat which he keeps at the harbour needs repairs. He sails it most weekends. His son who is ten loves the sea. They often sail together.","good":"Our neighbour owns a small boat. His boat, which he keeps at the harbour, needs repairs. He sails it most weekends. His son, who is ten, loves the sea. They often sail together.","explanation":"Extra information is separated by commas.","sentences":[{"bad":"Our neighbour owns a small boat.","good":"Our neighbour owns a small boat."},{"bad":"His boat which he keeps at the harbour needs repairs.","good":"His boat, which he keeps at the harbour, needs repairs."},{"bad":"He sails it most weekends.","good":"He sails it most weekends."},{"bad":"His son who is ten loves the sea.","good":"His son, who is ten, loves the sea."},{"bad":"They often sail together.","good":"They often sail together."}]},
      {"bad":"The café on the corner is popular. The owner who moved here last year serves great cakes. The queue is often long. The tables which are outside fill up first. It is worth the wait.","good":"The café on the corner is popular. The owner, who moved here last year, serves great cakes. The queue is often long. The tables, which are outside, fill up first. It is worth the wait.","explanation":"A non-defining clause goes between commas.","sentences":[{"bad":"The café on the corner is popular.","good":"The café on the corner is popular."},{"bad":"The owner who moved here last year serves great cakes.","good":"The owner, who moved here last year, serves great cakes."},{"bad":"The queue is often long.","good":"The queue is often long."},{"bad":"The tables which are outside fill up first.","good":"The tables, which are outside, fill up first."},{"bad":"It is worth the wait.","good":"It is worth the wait."}]},
      {"bad":"The book became a bestseller. The author who lives in this city wrote it quickly. She gave a talk at the library. The sequel which she is writing comes out next year. Fans are eagerly waiting.","good":"The book became a bestseller. The author, who lives in this city, wrote it quickly. She gave a talk at the library. The sequel, which she is writing, comes out next year. Fans are eagerly waiting.","explanation":"Set off the extra information with commas.","sentences":[{"bad":"The book became a bestseller.","good":"The book became a bestseller."},{"bad":"The author who lives in this city wrote it quickly.","good":"The author, who lives in this city, wrote it quickly."},{"bad":"She gave a talk at the library.","good":"She gave a talk at the library."},{"bad":"The sequel which she is writing comes out next year.","good":"The sequel, which she is writing, comes out next year."},{"bad":"Fans are eagerly waiting.","good":"Fans are eagerly waiting."}]}
