    "11.4": [
      {"bad":"My pen had run out of ink. Can you borrow me a pen? My friend handed me one. I promised to give it back, than I forgot. I returned it the next day.","good":"My pen had run out of ink. Can you lend me a pen? My friend handed me one. I promised to give it back, then I forgot. I returned it the next day.","explanation":"\"Lend\" gives and \"borrow\" receives; the sequence word is \"then\".","sentences":[{"bad":"My pen had run out of ink.","good":"My pen had run out of ink."},{"bad":"Can you borrow me a pen?","good":"Can you lend me a pen?"},{"bad":"My friend handed me one.","good":"My friend handed me one."},{"bad":"I promised to give it back, than I forgot.","good":"I promised to give it back, then I forgot."},{"bad":"I returned it the next day.","good":"I returned it the next day."}]},
      {"bad":"The dog looked tired after its walk. It wanted to lay down on the rug. It curled up by the fire. Please lay the blanket over it. It was soon fast asleep.","good":"The dog looked tired after its walk. It wanted to lie down on the rug. It curled up by the fire. Please lay the blanket over it. It was soon fast asleep.","explanation":"People and animals \"lie down\"; you \"lay\" something else down.","sentences":[{"bad":"The dog looked tired after its walk.","good":"The dog looked tired after its walk."},{"bad":"It wanted to lay down on the rug.","good":"It wanted to lie down on the rug."},{"bad":"It curled up by the fire.","good":"It curled up by the fire."},{"bad":"Please lay the blanket over it.","good":"Please lay the blanket over it."},{"bad":"It was soon fast asleep.","good":"It was soon fast asleep."}]},
      {"bad":"I felt unwell after lunch. I decided to lay down for an hour. The room was quiet and cool. I laid my book on the table first. I felt much better afterwards.","good":"I felt unwell after lunch. I decided to lie down for an hour. The room was quiet and cool. I laid my book on the table first. I felt much better afterwards.","explanation":"Use \"lie down\" for yourself and \"laid\" for placing an object.","sentences":[{"bad":"I felt unwell after lunch.","good":"I felt unwell after lunch."},{"bad":"I decided to lay down for an hour.","good":"I decided to lie down for an hour."},{"bad":"The room was quiet and cool.","good":"The room was quiet and cool."},{"bad":"I laid my book on the table first.","good":"I laid my book on the table first."},{"bad":"I felt much better afterwards.","good":"I felt much better afterwards."}]},
      {"bad":"The cat found a sunny spot. It likes to lay in the window. It sleeps there every afternoon. She laid a cushion on the sill for it. The cat was very comfortable.","good":"The cat found a sunny spot. It likes to lie in the window. It sleeps there every afternoon. She laid a cushion on the sill for it. The cat was very comfortable.","explanation":"\"Lie\" cannot take an object; \"lay\" needs an object.","sentences":[{"bad":"The cat found a sunny spot.","good":"The cat found a sunny spot."},{"bad":"It likes to lay in the window.","good":"It likes to lie in the window."},{"bad":"It sleeps there every afternoon.","good":"It sleeps there every afternoon."},{"bad":"She laid a cushion on the sill for it.","good":"She laid a cushion on the sill for it."},{"bad":"The cat was very comfortable.","good":"The cat was very comfortable."}]},
